[meta]
lang: en
title: OireMark conformance tests: Links
[/meta]

h1. Links

Tests for Section 7 of the specification.

h2. Basic Syntax

h3. Link on its own line {#links-basic}
[code om]
[Example]:https://example.com
[/code]
[code html]
<p><a href="https://example.com">Example</a></p>
[/code]

h3. Link inside a sentence {#links-in-sentence}
[code om]
Read [the docs]:https://example.com/docs now.
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Read <a href="https://example.com/docs">the docs</a> now.</p>
[/code]

h3. Escaped bracket inside link text {#links-escaped-bracket-in-text}
[code om]
[a \] b]:https://example.com
[/code]
[code html]
<p><a href="https://example.com">a ] b</a></p>
[/code]

h3. A bare URL is not a link {#links-bare-url-not-linked}
[code om]
Visit https://example.com today.
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Visit https://example.com today.</p>
[/code]

h3. Empty link text renders literally {#links-empty-text}
[code om]
[]:https://example.com
[/code]
[code html]
<p>[]:https://example.com</p>
[/code]

h2. Where a URL Ends

h3. URL ends at whitespace {#links-url-ends-at-space}
[code om]
[Example]:https://example.com/page and more
[/code]
[code html]
<p><a href="https://example.com/page">Example</a> and more</p>
[/code]

h3. URL ends at end of line {#links-url-ends-at-eol}
[code om]
[One]:https://example.com/one
[Two]:https://example.com/two
[/code]
[code html]
<p><a href="https://example.com/one">One</a><br>
<a href="https://example.com/two">Two</a></p>
[/code]

h3. Trailing period is not part of the URL {#links-trailing-period}
[code om]
See [the guide]:https://example.com/guide.
[/code]
[code html]
<p>See <a href="https://example.com/guide">the guide</a>.</p>
[/code]

h3. Other trailing punctuation is not part of the URL {#links-trailing-punctuation}
[code om]
Go [a]:https://example.com/a, now
Go [b]:https://example.com/b; now
Go [c]:https://example.com/c: now
Go [d]:https://example.com/d! now
Go [e]:https://example.com/e? now
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Go <a href="https://example.com/a">a</a>, now<br>
Go <a href="https://example.com/b">b</a>; now<br>
Go <a href="https://example.com/c">c</a>: now<br>
Go <a href="https://example.com/d">d</a>! now<br>
Go <a href="https://example.com/e">e</a>? now</p>
[/code]

h3. Trailing quotes are not part of the URL {#links-trailing-quotes}
[code om]
It is at '[the site]:https://example.com' now.
He said "[here]:https://example.com/x" twice.
[/code]
[code html]
<p>It is at '<a href="https://example.com">the site</a>' now.<br>
He said "<a href="https://example.com/x">here</a>" twice.</p>
[/code]

h3. Balanced parentheses stay in the URL {#links-balanced-parentheses}
[code om]
Read [the article]:https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mercury_(planet), then continue.
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Read <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mercury_(planet)">the article</a>, then continue.</p>
[/code]

h3. Unbalanced closing parenthesis is not part of the URL {#links-unbalanced-parenthesis}
[code om]
(see [the guide]:https://example.com/guide)
[/code]
[code html]
<p>(see <a href="https://example.com/guide">the guide</a>)</p>
[/code]

h3. Stripping repeats until nothing applies {#links-strip-repeated}
[code om]
(see [the guide]:https://example.com/guide.)
[/code]
[code html]
<p>(see <a href="https://example.com/guide">the guide</a>.)</p>
[/code]

h3. A link can end a bold span {#links-strip-bold-marker}
[code om]
*see [docs]:https://example.com*
[/code]
[code html]
<p><strong>see <a href="https://example.com">docs</a></strong></p>
[/code]

h3. A link can end an italic span before punctuation {#links-strip-italic-marker}
[code om]
_read [this]:https://example.com/x_.
[/code]
[code html]
<p><em>read <a href="https://example.com/x">this</a></em>.</p>
[/code]

h3. Formatting markers inside a URL are literal {#links-url-literal-markers}
[code om]
[Draft]:https://example.com/*draft*/page
[/code]
[code html]
<p><a href="https://example.com/*draft*/page">Draft</a></p>
[/code]

h3. Escapes inside a URL are literal {#links-url-literal-escapes}
[code om]
[Path]:https://example.com/a\_b/c
[/code]
[code html]
<p><a href="https://example.com/a\_b/c">Path</a></p>
[/code]

h3. Ampersand in a URL is escaped in the attribute {#links-url-ampersand}
[code om]
[Search]:https://example.com/?q=a&lang=en
[/code]
[code html]
<p><a href="https://example.com/?q=a&amp;lang=en">Search</a></p>
[/code]

h3. Percent-encoded trailing period is kept {#links-percent-encoded-period}
[code om]
[Version 1]:https://example.com/v1%2E
[/code]
[code html]
<p><a href="https://example.com/v1%2E">Version 1</a></p>
[/code]

h2. URL Normalization

h3. www gets https {#links-normalize-www}
[code om]
[Visit site]:www.example.com
[/code]
[code html]
<p><a href="https://www.example.com">Visit site</a></p>
[/code]

h3. Email address gets mailto {#links-normalize-email}
[code om]
[Contact us]:hello@example.com
[/code]
[code html]
<p><a href="mailto:hello@example.com">Contact us</a></p>
[/code]

h3. Email with subdomains {#links-normalize-email-subdomain}
[code om]
[Support]:support@mail.company.org
[/code]
[code html]
<p><a href="mailto:support@mail.company.org">Support</a></p>
[/code]

h3. Explicit mailto is unchanged {#links-normalize-mailto-unchanged}
[code om]
[Write]:mailto:hello@example.com
[/code]
[code html]
<p><a href="mailto:hello@example.com">Write</a></p>
[/code]

h3. Explicit http is unchanged {#links-normalize-http-unchanged}
[code om]
[Old site]:http://example.com
[/code]
[code html]
<p><a href="http://example.com">Old site</a></p>
[/code]

h3. tel scheme is unchanged {#links-normalize-tel}
[code om]
[Call us]:tel:+33123456789
[/code]
[code html]
<p><a href="tel:+33123456789">Call us</a></p>
[/code]

h3. Unknown schemes are unchanged {#links-normalize-unknown-schemes}
[code om]
[Open in app]:myapp://action/123

[Join call]:zoommtg://zoom.us/join?confno=123
[/code]
[code html]
<p><a href="myapp://action/123">Open in app</a></p>
<p><a href="zoommtg://zoom.us/join?confno=123">Join call</a></p>
[/code]

h3. Relative path is unchanged {#links-normalize-relative}
[code om]
[About]:/about

[Next]:./next-page
[/code]
[code html]
<p><a href="/about">About</a></p>
<p><a href="./next-page">Next</a></p>
[/code]

h3. Anchor is unchanged {#links-normalize-anchor}
[code om]
[Back to top]:#top
[/code]
[code html]
<p><a href="#top">Back to top</a></p>
[/code]

h3. A domain without www is a relative URL {#links-normalize-domain-without-www}
[code om]
[Site]:example.com
[/code]
[code html]
<p><a href="example.com">Site</a></p>
[/code]

h3. Scheme names may contain plus, hyphen and dot {#links-normalize-scheme-chars}
[code om]
[Repository]:git+ssh://example.com/repo.git
[/code]
[code html]
<p><a href="git+ssh://example.com/repo.git">Repository</a></p>
[/code]

h3. A host with a port and no // counts as a scheme {#links-normalize-host-port-scheme}
[code om]
[Local]:localhost:8080/page
[/code]
[code html]
<p><a href="localhost:8080/page">Local</a></p>
[/code]

h3. www is checked before scheme detection {#links-normalize-www-with-port}
[code om]
[Admin]:www.example.com:8080/x
[/code]
[code html]
<p><a href="https://www.example.com:8080/x">Admin</a></p>
[/code]

h3. Text with @ but no dot after it is not an email {#links-normalize-not-email}
[code om]
[Price]:price@50
[/code]
[code html]
<p><a href="price@50">Price</a></p>
[/code]

h2. Link Targets

h3. Web links get no target attribute {#links-no-target}
[code om]
[Secure]:https://example.com

[Plain]:http://example.com
[/code]
[code html]
<p><a href="https://example.com">Secure</a></p>
<p><a href="http://example.com">Plain</a></p>
[/code]

h2. Mentions

h3. Text starting with @ is a mention {#links-mention}
[code om]
[@Menelion]:https://dragonscave.space/@Menelion
[/code]
[code html]
<p><a href="https://dragonscave.space/@Menelion" class="mention">@Menelion</a></p>
[/code]

h3. Mention regardless of URL structure {#links-mention-any-url}
[code om]
[@jack]:https://bsky.app/profile/jack.bsky.social
[/code]
[code html]
<p><a href="https://bsky.app/profile/jack.bsky.social" class="mention">@jack</a></p>
[/code]

h3. @ later in the text is not a mention {#links-mention-not-first}
[code om]
[Ask @jack]:https://example.com/jack
[/code]
[code html]
<p><a href="https://example.com/jack">Ask @jack</a></p>
[/code]

h2. Link Text with Formatting

h3. Bold link text {#links-formatted-bold}
[code om]
[*Bold link text*]:https://example.com
[/code]
[code html]
<p><a href="https://example.com"><strong>Bold link text</strong></a></p>
[/code]

h3. Partly italic link text {#links-formatted-italic}
[code om]
[Visit _Example_]:https://example.com
[/code]
[code html]
<p><a href="https://example.com">Visit <em>Example</em></a></p>
[/code]

h2. Self-Linking URLs

h3. Self-link with www {#links-self-www}
[code om]
[www.example.com]
[/code]
[code html]
<p><a href="https://www.example.com">www.example.com</a></p>
[/code]

h3. Self-link with email {#links-self-email}
[code om]
[hello@example.com]
[/code]
[code html]
<p><a href="mailto:hello@example.com">hello@example.com</a></p>
[/code]

h3. Self-link with explicit scheme {#links-self-scheme}
[code om]
[https://example.com]
[/code]
[code html]
<p><a href="https://example.com">https://example.com</a></p>
[/code]

h3. Self-link with mailto keeps the written text {#links-self-mailto}
[code om]
[mailto:hello@example.com]
[/code]
[code html]
<p><a href="mailto:hello@example.com">mailto:hello@example.com</a></p>
[/code]

h3. Self-link inside a sentence {#links-self-in-sentence}
[code om]
Visit [https://example.com] today.
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Visit <a href="https://example.com">https://example.com</a> today.</p>
[/code]

h3. In a self-link nothing is stripped from the URL {#links-self-no-stripping}
[code om]
[https://example.com/guide.]
[/code]
[code html]
<p><a href="https://example.com/guide.">https://example.com/guide.</a></p>
[/code]

h3. Bracketed prose stays literal {#links-self-bracketed-prose}
[code om]
He said it was "irregardless" [sic].
As shown in [1], the result holds [citation needed].
[/code]
[code html]
<p>He said it was "irregardless" [sic].<br>
As shown in [1], the result holds [citation needed].</p>
[/code]

h3. Relative paths and anchors are not self-links {#links-self-relative-literal}
[code om]
Not links: [/about] and [#top]
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Not links: [/about] and [#top]</p>
[/code]

h2. Profiles

h3. Links in the inline profile are not wrapped in a paragraph {#links-profile-inline}
; profile
: inline
[code om]
[Example]:https://example.com
[/code]
[code html]
<a href="https://example.com">Example</a>
[/code]

h2. Unsafe URLs

h3. A javascript link is an error {#links-unsafe-javascript}
[code om]
Safe text.
[click]:javascript:alert(1)
[/code]
[code error]
unsafe-url 2
[/code]

h3. Letter case doesn't matter {#links-unsafe-mixed-case}
[code om]
[click]:JavaScript:alert(1)
[/code]
[code error]
unsafe-url 1
[/code]

h3. A vbscript link is an error {#links-unsafe-vbscript}
[code om]
[click]:vbscript:msgbox(1)
[/code]
[code error]
unsafe-url 1
[/code]

h3. A data image is an error {#links-unsafe-data-image}
[code om]
![Dot]:data:image/png;base64,AAAA
[/code]
[code error]
unsafe-url 1
[/code]

h3. A self-link with an unsafe scheme is an error {#links-unsafe-self-link}
[code om]
[javascript:alert(1)]
[/code]
[code error]
unsafe-url 1
[/code]

h3. A quote source with an unsafe scheme is an error {#links-unsafe-quote-source}
[code om]
[quote]:javascript:alert(1)
Quoted.
[/quote]
[/code]
[code error]
unsafe-url 1
[/code]

h3. A control character in a URL is an error {#links-unsafe-control-character}
The input is `[x]:a`, the control character U+0001, then `b`.
[code hex]
5B 78 5D 3A 61 01 62
[/code]
[code error]
unsafe-url 1
[/code]

h3. Only the scheme counts, not the word elsewhere in the URL {#links-unsafe-word-in-path}
[code om]
[Tutorial]:https://example.com/javascript:intro
[Guide]:/javascript:basics
[/code]
[code html]
<p><a href="https://example.com/javascript:intro">Tutorial</a><br>
<a href="/javascript:basics">Guide</a></p>
[/code]
